> You can just look at the altar. Or have I misunderstood the question?

Which is, incidentally, standing on the altar and hitting the : key
(far-look with ; doesn't work on Astral).  There's also a bug that
lets you determine it from a distance, by trying to "call" the priest
a name, but that's a bug exploit IMO.

Another think you can get a clue from is monster behavior--if monsters
are fleeing you in a temple, then it's the co-aligned altar.  If there
are monsters that normally flee (e.g. ants) that aren't fleeing, it's
the wrong altar.  That can save a few moves once you reach the temple.




